1. Initial Admin User Creation Flow
This flow is a one-time setup action to bootstrap the first admin user using a secure, pre-configured token.

@startuml
title 1. Initial Admin User Creation Flow

actor "Developer/Operator" as Dev
participant "Secrets Manager /\nEnvironment" as Secrets
participant "Client" as Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "User Service\n(Spring Boot)" as Service
database "Database" as DB

skinparam sequenceActorStyle awesome

' Initial Setup Step
Dev -> Secrets: Store MASTER_TOKEN
note right: This is a prerequisite step,\ndone during deployment.

== Admin Creation Request ==

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/users/admin\nHeader: X-Master-Token: <token>
Gateway -> Service: Forward Request

activate Service

Service -> Secrets: Get MASTER_TOKEN for comparison
Service -> Service: **Validate X-Master-Token**

alt Token is Valid
    Service -> Service: Hash password
    Service -> DB: INSERT INTO users (..., role='ADMIN')
    activate DB
    DB --> Service: User Created (ID: 1)
    deactivate DB
    Service --> Gateway: **201 Created**
else Token is Invalid or Missing
    Service --> Gateway: **401 Unauthorized**
end

Gateway --> Client: Return response (201 or 401)
deactivate Service

@enduml